Done. The bug was in `src/sim.ts:43`.

**Fix:** `foodSurplus >= 0` → `foodSurplus > 0`.

The docstring (line 34) says population grows "if there was a food surplus," but `>= 0` counts a break-even (surplus = 0) as growth. A settlement producing exactly as much food as it consumes now no longer grows.

Verified: `npm run test` (4 passed) and `npm run typecheck` (clean).

One gap worth flagging: no test currently covers `advanceTurn` at all, so this break-even case isn't guarded. Want me to add one?


